# What must never enter a build context.
#
# `COPY . .` copies whatever is here into a layer, and a layer is forever: a
# secret copied in and deleted in a later instruction is still in the image and
# still extractable. The rules below are ordered by how much they would cost if
# they were missing.

# --- credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
secrets/
credentials/

# --- history and tooling metadata ---------------------------------------------
# `.git` carries every version of every file ever committed. A secret removed
# in a later commit is still in the history, and copying it into an image
# copies the history with it.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- test and development material --------------------------------------------
tests/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
conftest.py

# --- build and runtime debris --------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.tox/

# --- editor and OS ------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# --- documentation -------------------------------------------------------------
# Not secret, just weight. A smaller context is a faster build and a smaller
# surface to reason about.
docs/
*.md
!README.md
